From: =?UTF-8?q?Do=C4=9Fukan=20Korkmazt=C3=BCrk?= <dkorkmazturk@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 07:50:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/38] Accept surface feedback tranches whose target matches
 our render device

OnSurfaceFeedbackTrancheDone is meant to keep the per-surface modifier
set from a tranche only when the tranche's target device is one of the
render devices the platform instance is rendering on. The condition was
inverted (`!=` instead of `==`), so a tranche whose target_device
matched our render device was rejected, and a tranche that did not
match was kept.

The end result was that per-surface tranches were dropped, and we fell
back to PickDefaultModifiers.

Flip the comparison so we keep tranches whose target_device matches one
of our render device ids, as the surrounding logic and the comments in
the function assume.
---
 src/wayland/wayland-surface.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/wayland-surface.c b/src/wayland/wayland-surface.c
index 543ba34..fa4ffcd 100644
--- a/src/wayland/wayland-surface.c
+++ b/src/wayland/wayland-surface.c
@@ -368,7 +368,7 @@ static void OnSurfaceFeedbackTrancheDone(void *userdata,
     {
         for (i=0; i<psurf->priv->inst->render_device_id_count; i++)
         {
-            if (state->base.tranche_target_device != psurf->priv->inst->render_device_id[i])
+            if (state->base.tranche_target_device == psurf->priv->inst->render_device_id[i])
             {
                 use_tranche = EGL_TRUE;
                 break;
